# oracle: fix colvars components angle (width 2), dihedral (periodic, 360), distanceZ (a fixed axis given as (1, 1, 0) and the ref-ref2 axis) and distanceXY (a fixed axis and the ref-ref2 axis) on the 256-atom LJ liquid of two masses; a harmonic restraint on the dihedral with a center 10 degrees away, and harmonicWalls: two walls with their own constants (lowerWallConstant/upperWallConstant, geometric-mean force constant) on angle and distanceZ, upper walls only on three distances, both walls on the periodic dihedral; fix_modify energy yes, two runs, the traj every 5 steps and the state every 20
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native: thermo 4.3e-15, final atoms 1.1e-13, traj and state files within 1e-10 (the dihedral uses Math.atan2 where native calls the C library atan2).
# oracle-inputs: w766cv_angles.colvars
# oracle-files: ang.colvars.traj ang.colvars.state
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 filerel=1e-10
units           lj
atom_modify     map array
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
set             atom 1*128 type 2
mass            1 1.0
mass            2 2.5
velocity        all create 1.5 87287 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0 2.5
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix             1 all nve
fix             2 all colvars w766cv_angles.colvars output ang
fix_modify      2 energy yes
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal f_2 f_2[1][1] f_2[2][1] f_2[3][1] f_2[4][1] f_2[5][1] f_2[6][1]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             40
run             20
